    "text": "Welcome\n\nGood documentation gives you a place to start and a path to follow. Rdocser brings your articles, architectural decisions, and presentations together in one connected workspace.\n\nChoose your path\n\nRead gives you a familiar documentation layout. Choose a topic from the sidebar, use the table of contents, and move between pages at your own pace.\n\nExplore opens a map of your documentation. Follow the connections, move cards around, and read several documents side by side.\n\nStart with Quick start, or learn how the pieces fit together in Architecture.\n\nMore than words on a page\n\nMDX lets you put working React components alongside your explanations. This example holds its own state—try it in an open graph card, then move or resize the card.\n\nFind what you need\n\nPress Ctrl K (or ⌘ K on a Mac) to search. Titles, collections, headings, and document text are all included. Select a result with the arrow keys and Enter.\n\nKeep exploring\n\nAuthoring documents explains frontmatter, links, and interactive content.Connected knowledge covers physics, cards, and sharing.Demo deck is a working Reveal.js presentation.",
