    "text": "Quick start\n\nRdocser reads your Markdown and MDX files and builds a browser-only documentation workspace.\n\nRun the workspace\n\nUse Node.js 22.12 or newer.\n\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n\nOpen the address printed by the development server. Changes to document content and metadata refresh the workspace automatically.\n\nAdd a document\n\nCreate a file under docs/. Folders become navigation collections unless you provide a group in frontmatter.\n\n---\ntitle: Your first guide\ngroup: Getting started\norder: 3\n---\n\n# Your first guide\n\nWrite something worth discovering.\n\nRead Authoring documents for links, code blocks, and interactive examples.\n\nBuild and preview\n\nnpm run build\nnpm run serve\n\nThe build produces static assets in dist/. Routing stays in the URL hash, so article links survive refreshes on GitHub Pages.\n\nCustomize your space\n\nChange the colors, font family, radius, or animation preference in theme.json. See Theme and accessibility.\n\nWhere to go next\n\nExplore Architecture or open Connected knowledge to learn how the document map works.",
