    "text": "Architecture\n\nRdocser separates pure domain concepts, application services, infrastructure adapters, and a thin React runtime. That keeps authoring, build tooling, and interaction logic from becoming entangled.\n\nFour layers\n\nLayerResponsibilityExamplesDomainStable document conceptsDocuments, relations, headingsApplicationDecisions and coordinationSearch, links, routing, share stateInfrastructureExternal systemsFilesystem scanner, Vite integration, persistenceRuntimeBrowser interactionReader, graph cards, Reveal decks\n\nServices and adapters are classes. UI components are functions that render state and dispatch actions.\n\nContent pipeline\n\nThe scanner walks the source directory, parses frontmatter, and reads Markdown headings and links from the syntax tree. The build adapter turns those projections into a typed manifest and lazy MDX imports.\n\nOnly the selected article and the content in open graph cards are loaded. Node positions are computed in a worker, keeping the reader responsive.\n\nClient-only runtime\n\nThe application owns its shell and hash routes. Rendering happens in the browser. Production output contains an HTML entry point, CSS, document chunks, and JavaScript assets.\n\nRead the project plan and subsequent ADRs for the rationale behind individual decisions.\n\nConnected documents\n\nOrdinary relative links and explicit frontmatter relations become graph edges. Follow Connected knowledge to see how the layout and shared state work.\n\nThe Demo deck presents these concepts interactively.",
