    "text": "Authoring documents\n\nUse Markdown for articles and MDX when you want to include React components. Content is trusted, author-owned source code.\n\nFrontmatter\n\n---\ntitle: A useful guide\ndescription: A short introduction for the document catalog.\ngroup: Guides\norder: 10\ntype: article\nrelations:\n  - target: guides/architecture\n    kind: explains\n---\n\nTitles fall back to the first level-one heading, then the filename. Groups fall back to the folder path. Document identifiers include their full path relative to the source directory.\n\nInvalid types, duplicate identifiers, and missing explicit relation targets stop the build with the source filename in the error.\n\nRelative links\n\nLink to another source file using its path:\n\n[Architecture](./architecture.mdx)\n[Four layers](./architecture.mdx#four-layers)\n\nThe reader resolves these to hash routes. Graph cards open linked documents within the graph. Links inside code fences are examples, not graph connections.\n\nInteractive React\n\nImport a component into MDX, or export a small component directly from the document. Its state belongs to that mounted document instance. Dragging and resizing an open card preserves it.\n\nThe Welcome article includes an interactive counter.\n\nPresentations\n\nSet type: presentation and use Deck, Slide, Stack, and Fragment in MDX. Rdocser provides those components automatically.\n\n<Deck>\n  <Slide>\n    <h1>An idea worth sharing</h1>\n  </Slide>\n  <Slide>\n    <h2>One step at a time</h2>\n    <Fragment><p>Reveal the next thought.</p></Fragment>\n  </Slide>\n</Deck>\n\nTry the Demo deck.",
