    "text": "Theme and accessibility\n\nA few design tokens define the entire workspace. The same palette flows through the reader, graph, dialogs, and presentation controls.\n\nTheme tokens\n\nEdit theme.json at the project root.\n\n{\n  \"colors\": {\n    \"background\": \"#fafaf9\",\n    \"foreground\": \"#202321\",\n    \"primary\": \"#35624d\",\n    \"muted\": \"#6e746f\",\n    \"card\": \"#ffffff\"\n  },\n  \"radius\": \"0.625rem\",\n  \"animation\": true\n}\n\nChoose a foreground and background with sufficient contrast. Define primary-foreground when you use a light primary color.\n\nKeyboard navigation\n\nTab moves through the navigation and controls. Arrow keys switch view choices and move through search results. Enter opens the selected result, and Escape closes dialogs.\n\nThe Skip to content link appears when focused. The sidebar separator can be adjusted with the keyboard.\n\nSmaller screens\n\nNavigation opens in a focus-managed sheet on phones. The reader keeps its comfortable line length; tables and code blocks scroll within the content instead of stretching the page.\n\nMotion preferences\n\nSet animation: false to reduce interface motion. The workspace also respects the system's reduced-motion preference. Graph physics starts paused when reduced motion is requested.\n\nPresentations\n\nEach deck owns its keyboard focus. Focus a presentation before using arrow keys. Two open decks keep their slide position and listeners independent.\n\nTry Demo deck and A second perspective together in the graph.",
